    [Plan #35 Phase 4 close] V3 empirical A/B + verifier-barrier interaction fix. Empirical result: round-1 cross-leak count goes from v1=4, v2=6 to v3=0 — agents produce truly independent round-1 positions under the barrier. Both v2 cascade and v3 barrier reach productive_disagreement at round 3 (expected per literature; 2603.28813 reports WR has higher peer-reference rate but lower consensus than CR). v3 synthesis identifies semantic-support verification as the new #1 priority — exactly the gap Plan #34 had deferred to Plan #37 — confirming the barrier closed v2 highest-leverage gap. Interaction fix: _lineage_entries fabricated_peer_ref check was reading peer state from latest_positions[peer], which under the barrier produced 7 false positives in v3 round 2 (agents legitimately referenced peer round-1 claim_ids that the peer had renamed in round 2; verifier compared against the renamed ids and flagged real references as fabricated). Now reads from prior_positions_by_agent[peer] for round_num greater than 1, matching what the agent actually saw under the barrier. For round 1 the verifier passes an empty position so any peer reference still fires as fabricated (peer should have written nothing). Tests unchanged (existing tests set round=2 with empty prior dict which now resolves to empty peer position — same semantics). Verifier rerun on v3 yields silent_retire=7, fabricated_peer_ref=0 (down from 7 false positives). retro_verify_v3.py + comparison_deliberation_runs.py expanded. 43/43 deliberation tests pass after the fix.

